          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.501,
            0.849,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Can you construct a triangle all of whose angles are equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 0 ^ { \\circ } ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If two of the angles are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " what would the third angle be? If all the angles in a triangle have to be equal, then what must its measure be? Explore and find out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.581,
            0.63,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Here is a triangle in which we know "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathbf{B} = \\angle \\mathbf{C}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle A = 50^{\\circ}."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Can you find ∠B and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle C ?"
